{
  "action": "lock_tin",
  "note": "Thirty-five seconds, acoustic window clear, public speaker already dead. Phil pulled the plug on the room speaker right before the splice hit the head, so nothing leaked. The tin is in my tray, seal intact, the way it should be. I'm not sending it to the copy desk. That outtake — \"Your mic is still on, Mercury\" — is not a public record. It's my brother's tape, my name on it in a room where I didn't want a name. I lock 5066, I keep the key in my palm, and I decide later, on my schedule, how much of that ident the morning air hears. The distinctive broadcast I promised is the ident, clean, not the flinch after it. The archive belongs to me. It stays in my drawer."
}
